    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d677">

                <pb facs="0734" n="722" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg722"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.8830 Coal/234: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-02-09T22:00:00-03:00">February 9, 1943—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>689. Department’s 476, February 8, 5 p.m. The effect on Brazilian economy
                    especially transportation would be decidedly unfavorable. Minister of
                        Finance<anchor n="36" xml:id="d677-f1"/> and Secretary of President
                        Vargas<anchor n="37" xml:id="d677-f2"/> yesterday <pb facs="0735" n="723"
                        xml:id="pg723"/> strongly criticized our unilateral action in reducing
                    shipment to 50,000 tons and requested an increase. They were told that the
                    Embassy could not recommend a figure in excess of 50,000 tons monthly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
